Z||000017||Ryan Wright||08-13-2001||07:14 PM||||Aus, I spoke with you via private email, but I'll say it again here: You have some amazing products at even more amazing prices. I'll definitely be a future customer.<P>For advertising: Get some info out to the Fiero lists. <A HREF="http://www.fiero.org," TARGET=_blank>www.fiero.org,</A>  and head to V8 Archie's Technet at <A HREF="http://www.v8archie.com." TARGET=_blank>www.v8archie.com.</A>  I've been an active member of the Fiero list for over 5 years, and of Technet since it's birth. You should be able to grab a handful of customers there. When I get around to putting an actual Fiero web site back online, I'll certainly put a link up for you.<P>Good luck! We're behind you all the way!<BR><P>------------------<BR>-Ryan Wright (http://www.ryanwright.com)||||reg||1
Z||000018||Cheever2||08-13-2001||07:48 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Galen:<BR><B>would anyone like a searchable (yahoo like) database of Fiero Clubs worldwide?</B><BR><HR></BLOCKQUOTE>Absolutely!  The best I could do was by spending countless hours looking at all the clubs' links for other clubs, then checking for <I>their</I> links.  My list is in this archived thread: <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000002/HTML/20010706-1-004529.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000002/HTML/20010706-1-004529.html</A> <P>I was not able to keep it updated.  Sorry.  Hope you have something better.<P><BR><p>[This message has been edited by Cheever2 (edited 08-13-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000019||rogergarrison||08-13-2001||07:54 PM||||Good luck to you Aus. What kinds of export taxes and such for us in the USA, whats rate of exchange, shipping, wait time etc. Just rough estimates in case I want to order anything in future.||||reg||1
Z||000020||AusFiero||08-13-2001||08:10 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by rogergarrison:<BR><B>Good luck to you Aus. What kinds of export taxes and such for us in the USA, whats rate of exchange, shipping, wait time etc. Just rough estimates in case I want to order anything in future.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I quote everything in my store in US$$$s Roger and always include delivery in the price. At my end I have no export taxes. From the USA customs site most items under $1000 going into the USA attract no import duty. If unlucky to get a customs official having a b!tch of a day you will get slugged 2.5%. Best checked at your end but I searched for hours and thats all it seems to be. Delivery times to keep items cheaper depend on the item. Stage 2 parts are based on 2 to 4 weeks delivery but I also give the option of 3 to 10 days for slightly more. If people ws really urgently needing something I can get 1 to 2 day delivery but that is not cheap. Most other products are covered by the 3 to 10 days option. <P>Thanks everyone else for the support and the Fiero links and information about clubs.<P>IwannaIRM I would definately appreciate that book if it has clubs in it. I would look after you in the future in exchange. I will email you.<P>Ferrari_Momo, yes we will do business on those parts I can get for you. <P>Also sorry to people for some delays at present on things that have been ordered. I have been snowed under with requests and have been trying to set all this up and trying to rest all at once, its a fine balance. Am recovering fast now. Another 4 weeks I think and then I will be full bore again. Stage 2 scoops are almost there now. Other bits I have been catching up on. I know who has had to wait what I feel is a little too ling but be assured I remember the patient people and will look after them well in the future with discounts or the odd freebie etc. Thanks guys and gals.<P>Time to go back to the bodykit, Will get some pictures up tomorrow of how it is going along as hopefully my USB port is getting fixed tomorrow and I can get things out of my camera.<P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.auto-alley.com" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
Z||000021||Cheever2||08-13-2001||08:15 PM||||I bet I wouldn't be the first to ask if I can have a job.  Making a living doing something related to Fieros, and living in Australia... sounds good to me!<BR> <A HREF="http://www.tourismwollongong.com/regions/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.tourismwollongong.com/regions/</A> <BR><p>[This message has been edited by Cheever2 (edited 08-13-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000022||Archie||08-13-2001||08:27 PM||||Congrats on jumping into the fire. <P>I would have advised you to pick a different name. Like Aus WorldWide Fiero or something like that. IMHO, picking "Fiero Shop" is kinda like poking a stick in your eye on the first day of a new job.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Anyway, you'll do fine.<P>Archie||||reg||1
Z||000023||AusFiero||08-13-2001||08:35 PM||||Actually I only chose that name Archie because a guy over here already had been using it and was silly enough not to grab the domain name. I will probably add Australia or the Worldwide sounds good too onto the end of it for advertising purposes. I don't want to be mixed up with the other 2 Fiero Shops but it was too good to pass up. To get domain names in Australia you must be a business and the name must pertain to your business. Wll be grabbing <A HREF="http://www.fiero.com.au" TARGET=_blank>www.fiero.com.au</A>  next. That I don't know what I will use for yet. Will also be pointing out on the website that I have no affiliation with the American or Canadian stores. Something I notice neither of them do on their sites.<BR>  Now back to it I supppose, can hear my email notification out in the garage  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Will be glad when I get everything down to the workshop and can actually just go to work then come home.||||reg||1
Z||000024||DXR_DAD||08-13-2001||09:30 PM||||Good luck Aus, you have started out with a GOOD REP!!! you business should go far.<BR>I've noticed how well you keep your customer informed as to whats going on and updates on the progress of orders and what not, That's a good thing!!!  Keep up the good work<P>DXR_DAD||||reg||14
